{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I will break the pride of your might.</b> This is the Temple. And thus it says: ״הִנְנִי מְחַלֵּל אֶת מִקְדָּשִׁי גְּאוֹן עֻזְּכֶם״ (Ezekiel 24)." "<b>And I will make your heaven as iron and your earth as bronze.</b> This is harsher than what Moses said, for there he says: ״וְהָיוּ שָׁמֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר עַל רֹאשְׁךָ נְחֹשֶׁת וגו׳״ (Deuteronomy 28) — that the heavens would sweat as bronze sweats, but the earth would not sweat as iron does not sweat, and it keeps its fruits. But here the heavens would not sweat as iron does not sweat, and there would be drought in the world, and the earth would sweat as bronze sweats, and it destroys its fruits (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:41.538777549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}